The symcli outputs of the om3 driver tests (drivers/arraysymmetrix/testdata),
in the sections v2 pushed them under, made to agree on their devices:
sym_dev_info is synthesized to hold every device the other outputs name, and
sym_dev_wwn_info, sym_meta_info, sym_ficondev_info and sym_sg_info gained the
entries of those devices. Not captured from an array.

The rows TestParseSymmetrix expects are the ones insert_sym made of these
outputs, with the collector init/modules/symmetrix.py run under python 2.7.
